---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
	</head>
	<body class="home">
		<Header />
		<main>
			<div class="prose">
				<p>
					Hi, I'm Nick. I'm a software engineer at
					<a href="https://funnel.io">Funnel</a>, building surprisingly smart
					tools for marketing teams. Before that I spent some time at Klarna.
				</p>
				<p>
					These days most of my code gets written with coding agents, so that's
					mostly what I <a href="/thoughts">write about</a>: what works, what
					doesn't, and the tools I build to make it less painful. The
					<a href="/harness">harness</a> is my current setup, taken apart piece
					by piece.
				</p>
				<p>
					On the side I build <a href="/works">small dev tools</a>.
					<a href="https://github.com/nicksenap/grove">Grove</a> manages git
					worktrees across multiple repos, and
					<a href="https://github.com/nicksenap/paparazzi">Paparazzi</a> lets
					coding agents see what's in your browser.
				</p>
			</div>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
